# Senka — production credentials, loaded by hand.
#
# Nothing loads this file automatically — not Next, not Eve. It exists so you
# can point a local shell at the real production database and bucket on
# purpose, when you need to, without ever writing those credentials into
# `.env` or `.env.local`:
#
#   set -a; . ./.env.prod; set +a; pnpm dev
#
# Real shell variables still win over `.env.local`. This file is gitignored —
# never commit it with real values. Be deliberate about what you run while it
# is loaded: it is the same database and bucket the deployed site uses, so a
# delete here is a real delete.
#
# This file is NOT part of the Ansible deployment in deploy/ — the deployed
# host gets its own environment from systemd/Ansible, independently of this.
# This is only for an operator's local shell.

# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Use the SESSION pooler port, not the transaction pooler. The Workflow world
# runs on graphile-worker, which depends on LISTEN/NOTIFY and session-scoped
# advisory locks — the transaction pooler silently drops both, so the queue
# stalls with no error while /api/health still reports `store: true`. On
# Supabase that's port 5432 for the session pooler, not 6543.
WORKFLOW_POSTGRES_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/database"

# ── Connection budget ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Budget against the pooler's client limit (Supabase's session pooler ships at
# 15), not the database's max_connections. The app opens four of its own pools
# plus the Workflow world's, and `pnpm dev` runs two processes (Next and Eve)
# each holding a full set — so the default of 5 per pool overruns a small
# pooler fast. Lower both until (pools + world) × processes stays under the
# pooler's limit.
STEVE_PG_MAX_POOL_SIZE="2"
WORKFLOW_POSTGRES_MAX_POOL_SIZE="2"

# ── File storage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keep the bucket PRIVATE — reads come back through the app, nothing here
# mints a public URL.
S3_ENDPOINT="https://your-project.storage.supabase.co/storage/v1/s3"
S3_REGION="us-east-1"
S3_BUCKET="media"
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID="replace-with-a-real-access-key-id"
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY="replace-with-a-real-secret-access-key"
